### M0033 §0.3 [REQUIREMENT] REQ-DLV-005;REQ-DLV-013
  TEXT: A reviewer must not be an implementation author for the reviewed scope, even under another agent name. Record the agent role, actual invocation/run reference if exposed, reviewed revision, assignment and independence declaration. If the runtime exposes no stable run ID, preserve the distinct invocation evidence and state that limitation; do not invent provider identifiers. Independence means separate real agent work, not a guarantee of error-free results or different model providers.
  -> REQ-DLV-005 [ENGINEERING] Apply each role's independence rule at every gate: no role reviews, certifies or approves its own work, and the orchestrator never records a review verdict | final DG7
  -> REQ-DLV-013 [ENGINEERING] Define the review record contract and verify provenance: role, candidate, invocation reference, implementation author, independence declaration, requirements checked, checks run, findings, verdict, ev | final DG0

### M0039 §0.4 [REQUIREMENT] REQ-DLV-014
  TEXT: 4. Review: invoke all three independent reviewers against that candidate. For visible changes, review rendered screens in Arabic and English as well as code.
  -> REQ-DLV-014 [ENGINEERING] Run the eight-step gate loop for every stage: plan, implement, integrate and freeze, review (rendered Arabic and English screens for visible changes), record findings, repair, reverify, audit | final DG7

### M0044 §0.4 [REQUIREMENT] REQ-DLV-015
  TEXT: Gate states are PLANNED → BUILDING → REVIEWING → FIXING → VERIFYING → APPROVED; a failure or external dependency can set BLOCKED. A stage with no findings may go from REVIEWING to VERIFYING. No time limit, majority vote, high average score or implementer’s confidence can turn FAIL/BLOCKED into approval.
  -> REQ-DLV-015 [ENGINEERING] Implement the gate state machine PLANNED, BUILDING, REVIEWING, FIXING, VERIFYING, APPROVED (BLOCKED on failure or external dependency) and never convert FAIL/BLOCKED into approval by time, vote, score | final DG0

